Subject: Re: [stan-users] [Whishlist] Ability to export a quantity computed in the "model" part of a Stan model
Message-ID: <yeBZKoCv89k.sQqzOsqZ55YJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <yeBZKoCv89k.nGCM4qsdJ9wJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <yeBZKoCv89k.nGCM4qsdJ9wJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/yeBZKoCv89k/m/sQqzOsqZ55YJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Other people have asked for this, too.

Basically, the idea is to completely get rid of the transformed
paramters block and instead flag variables declared at the top of
the model block as save or no save.

Right now, the transformed parameters may depend on "uninteresting"
quantities, as in

  transformed parameters {
    real a;
    real b;
    {
       real c;  // uninteresting
       real d;  // uninteresting

       ... define a and b ...
    }
  }

but the uninteresting variables will not be available in the model
block.

The alternative that makes most sense to me would be this:

  model {
    save real a;
    save real b;
    real c;
    real d;
    ....
  }

- Bob

