> Error in if (!missing(bandwidth) && min(bandwidth) <= 0) stop("'bandwidth' must be strictly positive") :

It comes from the first line of KernSmooth::bkde2D, which is called by grDevices:::.smoothScatterCalcDensity and autocalculates the bandwidth via

        bandwidth <- diff(apply(x, 2, quantile, probs = c(0.05,
            0.95), na.rm = TRUE, names = FALSE))/25

>   missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed
> In addition: Warning messages:
> 1: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf
> 2: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf
> 3: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf
> 4: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf

Is it possible that two consecutive theta values overflowed to Inf? Does

all(is.finite(as.array(fit)))

return TRUE?

Ben

