Sorry to just now be getting to this. The problem is that theta_4 was commented out of the model and whatever version of rstan you used had a bug in pairs about catching non-existent parameters that somehow got fixed along the way. In any event,

pairs(fit, pars = c("theta_1", "theta_2", "theta_3"))

should work but for diagnostic purposes, you usually want to add "lp__" to pars and condition = "something" to the arguments, where "something" is (a unique abbreviation of) the name of one of the extra parameters like accept_stat__ .

Ben

