AAAaaaaahhhhhh!!  Now I get it. (Or at least, I think that I have it now.)  I had either missed or not understood that declaration. b is a length T vector of N length vectors.  Then, since b1 is only N long, the draws for those numbers have to be the same for all 4 estimates of log(y) at each level of N (patient offset).  b has N  * T draws, so that the each of the four estimates of log(y) can have a separate draw (patient * visit offset).  .

I had missed that, or perhaps misunderstood it.  "Now is the way clear!" (TS Eliot)

