The advantage of running 4 chains rather than 1 is that you can easily diagnose convergence.  With only 1 chain it’s hard to tell what’s going on.  Especially when testing and debugging when you’re trying different things.  You might be able to run 4 chains for 100 iterations each instead of nervously running 1 chain for 2000 iterations, for example.

> On Jun 15, 2015, at 12:20 PM, Andrew Verdin <andrew...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> What would running 4 chains (as opposed to 1 chain) do differently?  I typically run only one chain when I am testing and debugging my models.
