Indeed it is pretty impressive!

Another quick Q: would it be worthwhile to reparameterize my model so that all normal distributions are standard normal? I've already got the Cholesky reparameterization going on for the multinormal, but what about for my gamma priors

  gamma[1,1] ~ normal(6, 5);
  gamma[1,2] ~ normal(4, 5);
  gamma[1,3] ~ normal(0, 2);
  gamma[2] ~ normal(0,5);

and the following line:
  y ~ normal(Mod_jj, sigma);

it seems like changing these to normal(0,1)'s is too trivial to affect the parameterization of the model & its speed, but I'm not sure if there's something I'm missing here about the virtues of sampling std normals.

