>
> From my loose knowledge, empirical likelihood takes the place of a parametric likelihood.
>
> Instead of using the implied probabilities of an analytic parametric likelihood, we need to impose moment constraints (means and variances) and optimizes over the simplex to obtain the probability "jumps"
>
> The implementations I've seen coded in [R] does this using the various optim() functions
>
