The 10K version seems to have converged, but the 70K obviously
hasn't. And variables like tau[1] seem stuck in different modes.

All I can suggest from looking at this is to (a) start with
a smaller step size, (b) target a higher acceptance rate, and (c)
run longer.

If it's truly multimodal it won't help---maybe just plotting the
after-convergence bit of lp__ would show the densities are way off.
Hard to tell with the warmup skewing the scale.

